# ◈ packages.kde-qt.list — Qt5 / KDE Frameworks stack + partitioning tools
#
# RENAMED from packages.calamares.list — Calamares itself was dropped (kept
# hitting REQUIRED_USE/python-target churn and was ultimately not wanted for
# the ISO), but everything else in this list already builds cleanly on its
# own, so it stayed rather than being thrown out along with Calamares.
# Keeping the "kde-qt" name rather than "calamares" now that the actual
# installer isn't in here avoids the file being misleading later.
#
# ASSUMPTION (flag if wrong): Qt5 + KDE Frameworks 5, not Qt6/KF6. Rationale —
# Qt5/KF5 has a longer track record building under musl. Worth revisiting
# once KF6 musl builds are more battle-tested elsewhere.
#
# If none of this ends up used for anything else either, it's a clean
# one-line removal per package the same way calamares was removed below —
# no need to keep dependencies around "just in case" once nothing needs them.

dev-qt/qtcore
dev-qt/qtgui
dev-qt/qtwidgets
dev-qt/qtnetwork
dev-qt/qtsvg
dev-qt/qtdeclarative
dev-qt/qtquickcontrols2
dev-qt/qtwayland
dev-qt/qttranslations
dev-qt/qtdbus

kde-frameworks/extra-cmake-modules
kde-frameworks/kcoreaddons
kde-frameworks/kconfig
kde-frameworks/kconfigwidgets
kde-frameworks/kwidgetsaddons
kde-frameworks/kiconthemes
kde-frameworks/ki18n
kde-frameworks/solid
kde-frameworks/kservice
kde-frameworks/kpackage

sys-libs/kpmcore
sys-block/parted
sys-fs/lvm2
sys-fs/cryptsetup
sys-fs/e2fsprogs
sys-fs/dosfstools
sys-fs/ntfs3g

sys-auth/polkit
dev-cpp/yaml-cpp
dev-libs/boost
